  "ts": "2026-05-28T06:05:15.672186Z",
  "content": "Distribution flow: `yullu install [target...] [--service|--yes|--no-service]` is the canonical onboarding command. Targets: claude (auto-detected from ~/.claude), codex (auto-detected from ~/.codex), cursor (explicit only — ~/.cursor is shared with VS Code Cursor IDE). What each install does: Claude → SKILL.md + claude mcp add + Stop hook entry in ~/.claude/settings.json (deterministic record_messages via 'yullu record-turn' subcommand). Codex → AGENTS.md skill section + [mcp_servers.yullu] in ~/.codex/config.toml. Cursor → ~/.cursor/mcp.json entry + printed rules snippet (no hooks support in Cursor). Service install (prompted by default, --service to skip prompt): launchd plist on macOS (~/Library/LaunchAgents/ai.yullu.server.plist, RunAtLoad+KeepAlive), systemd user unit on Linux (~/.config/systemd/user/yullu.service). Windows skipped with a clear message. Everything merges with existing user config (don't clobber) and is fully reversed by `yullu uninstall`. POST /api/messages is the REST entry point hooks use to feed the session buffer — same code path as the MCP record_messages tool.\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003ctags\u003e[\"distribution\", \"install\", \"hooks\", \"architecture\"]\u003c/tags\u003e",
